                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>This could be a Mr Robotham who is a leading actor in a
                            number of plays in this period, and is seen in the company of a number
                            of Godwin's friends from the theatre. Probably introduced by Junius Booth.  But it might also be Thomas Leeson Scrase Rowbotham (1782-1853), professor of drawing at the Royal Naval School, New Cross. 
                        The forst four contacts are in August 1824. Booth calls and then Booth and Robotham suup (23 Aug); Godwin writes to Rowbotham (26 Aug); he calls on Rowbotham (30 Aug) and on Aug 3`1 Rowbotham and W[illiam] sup.  This looks a familiar pattern of trying to recruit William to some profession.  That does not seem to have worked,in this as in other instances,.
                        </p>
